National Defense Authorization Act for Fiscal Year 2024

SECTION 1201. INDO-PACIFIC SECURITY ASSISTANCE.

(a) AUTHORIZATION OF APPROPRIATIONS.—There is authorized to be appropriated $2,000,000,000 for fiscal year 2024 for the Indo-Pacific Security Initiative to support the following activities:
(1) bilateral and multilateral military exercises with allies and partners in the Indo-Pacific region, including Japan, Australia, the Republic of Korea, the Philippines, and India;
(2) deployment of additional naval assets and rotational forces to United States Indo-Pacific Command;
(3) improvements to forward-deployed infrastructure, including airfield upgrades in Guam, the Commonwealth of the Northern Mariana Islands, and Palau;
(4) foreign military financing for Taiwan under the Taiwan Enhanced Resilience Act.

(b) REPORT.—Not later than 180 days after the date of the enactment of this Act, the Secretary of Defense, in coordination with the Secretary of State, shall submit to the congressional defense committees a report on the implementation of the strategy required by section 1251 of the National Defense Authorization Act for Fiscal Year 2023 (Public Law 117-263).

Sponsor: Rep. Mike Rogers [R-AL-3]. Chair, House Armed Services Committee.
